(a) Smoking and drinking prohibited on MARTA buses, trains, rail cars and paid areas. It shall be unlawful for occupants of Metropolitan Atlanta Rapid Transit Authority (MARTA) buses, trains or rail cars to smoke tobacco or consume alcoholic beverages while such buses, trains or rail cars are transporting passengers within the corporate limits of the City or within paid areas adjacent thereto. Charter bus service is excluded from these restrictions.
(b) Evading payment of fare for transportation service. It shall be unlawful, within the corporate limits of the City, for any person to evade or attempt to evade payment of the fare for transportation service upon the Metropolitan Atlanta Rapid Transit Authority rapid rail system or public transit bus. As used in this section, "evasion of payment of fare" shall include the following acts, activities or conduct:
(1) Entry into a paid area or upon a rapid rail car of public transit bus without payment of the fare charged for transportation service;
(2) Misuse of a transfer, TransCard, pass, ticket, token, or other evidence of payment of or prepayment of a fare issued by the Metropolitan Atlanta Rapid Transit Authority ("MARTA") with the intent to avoid or to assist another in avoiding payment of the fare charged for transportation service;
(3) Use or attempted use of a signed MARTA TransCard for the payment of the fare charged for transportation service by a person who is not the person whose signature appears on the TransCard.
(Ord. No. 92-10, § 1, 12-7-92)

